<article class="col-lg-8 offset-lg-1">
<div class="privacy-note"><p class="eyebrow">HS &amp; CO Counsellors at Law</p><p class="mb-0">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-30">30 October 2026</time>. This policy covers the HSNCO website and its account activation, authentication and email delivery features.</p></div>
<section id="privacy-scope"><h2>1. About this policy</h2><p>HS &amp; CO Counsellors at Law (HSNCO, ?we?, ?us? or ?our?) explains here how information is handled through our website and its administration application. This policy concerns website use and initial enquiries. Any separate engagement terms and confidentiality arrangements governing legal services continue to apply.</p><p>Google account authorisation is used to connect an approved sending mailbox for website email delivery. Visitors and recipients do not need to grant HSNCO access to their Google accounts to receive an activation message or verification code.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-information"><h2>2. Information we collect</h2><ul><li><strong>Enquiries:</strong> your name, email address, optional telephone number, selected legal service and the message you submit.</li><li><strong>Account information:</strong> an authorised user's name, email address, role, account status, password hash, activation and verification records.</li><li><strong>Technical and security information:</strong> IP address, browser information, session identifiers, authentication events and security logs used to operate and protect the application.</li><li><strong>Google connection information:</strong> the approved sender's verified email identity and OAuth credentials described below.</li></ul><p>Please do not submit sensitive case documents, identification documents or confidential details through an initial website enquiry. Submitting an enquiry does not by itself establish a lawyer-client relationship.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-purposes"><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>We use submitted information to review and respond to enquiries, administer authorised accounts, deliver activation links and one-time verification codes, send configured operational notifications, maintain website security and investigate technical issues.</p><p>Session cookies support authentication and request security. Where a user chooses to trust a device, a security cookie helps recognise that browser during its configured validity period. Blocking or clearing these cookies may require signing in or verifying the device again.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-google"><h2>4. Google account and Gmail access</h2><p>An authorised administrator connects the approved sending mailbox through Google's OAuth consent process. The application requests <code>openid</code> and <code>email</code> to verify the sender's identity, and <code>gmail.send</code> to send email on behalf of that mailbox.</p><p>Google data used by this integration includes the sender's email identity, access and refresh tokens, token expiry information and the message data submitted for delivery, such as recipient addresses, subjects and message bodies. It is used to authenticate the sending mailbox and deliver account activation emails, verification codes and configured website notifications.</p><p>The integration does not request permission to read the sender's inbox, search existing messages, access contacts or access Google Drive files. It does not request access to recipients' Google accounts. OAuth tokens are stored encrypted in the application database; passwords for the Google account are not collected by HSNCO.</p><p>Google user data is not used for advertising, sold, or used to train general-purpose artificial intelligence or machine-learning models. Access is limited to providing, maintaining and securing the described integration, handling an authorised support request or meeting a legal obligation. HSNCO's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-sharing"><h2>5. Sharing and service providers</h2><p>Enquiries and account records are available to authorised HSNCO personnel according to their responsibilities. Website hosting and database providers process information needed to operate the service. Google processes email information when Gmail delivery is used; recipients receive the messages addressed to them.</p><p>Information may also be disclosed where required by applicable law or necessary to investigate abuse and protect legal rights. We do not sell personal information. Hosting and email services may process information in countries other than your own, subject to their service arrangements.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-security"><h2>6. Storage and security</h2><p>Information is stored in the application database and server storage, with access controls for administrative functions. Passwords and verification codes are stored as hashes; Gmail OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest by the application. Production connections are intended to use HTTPS.</p><p>These measures reduce risk but cannot guarantee absolute security. Keep activation links, verification codes and account credentials private. Operational backups or email copies, where maintained, must also be considered when handling a deletion request.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-retention"><h2>7. Retention</h2><p>We retain enquiries for follow-up and administration according to the configured retention process. Account, authentication and security records are retained as needed to provide access, investigate incidents and meet applicable obligations. Expired authentication credentials cannot be used to complete verification, although associated audit records may remain.</p><p>Google connection credentials are retained while the sending mailbox remains connected. Disconnecting the integration and removing its stored credentials stops future authorised sending through that connection. Deleting information from this application does not delete copies already delivered to a recipient or stored by an external provider.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-choices"><h2>8. Your choices and requests</h2><p>You may contact HSNCO to request access to, correction of or deletion of information you have provided, or to raise a privacy concern. We may verify your identity before acting and may retain information where required for a lawful obligation or an unresolved matter.</p><p>The owner of the connected sending mailbox can revoke HSNCO's access through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account connections</a>. They can also request that HSNCO remove the stored Google connection credentials. Revoking access disables email delivery through that mailbox until a new authorisation is completed.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-external"><h2>9. External services</h2><p>External links, including LinkedIn, and map content or links may direct your browser to third-party services. Those services may receive technical information such as your IP address and apply their own privacy and cookie policies. This policy does not govern those external websites.</p></section>
<section id="privacy-contact"><h2>10. Contact and policy updates</h2><p>For privacy questions, Google connection removal or a request concerning your information, use our <a href="{{ route('contact') }}#enquiry">contact form</a> and identify your message as a privacy request. Do not include passwords, tokens or verification codes.</p><p>We will update this page when our information-handling practices change. The date above identifies the latest revision. Material changes to Google data access or usage will be reflected in this policy and, where required, in the authorisation process.</p></section>
